 order with at least one line, positive pack quantities, an organisation-owned address, and an idempotency key.\",\n     \"when\": \"The order is submitted twice with the same key and payload.\",\n     \"then\": \"Both response bodies return the same order identifier and the order list contains one order.\",\n     \"level\": \"api\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"id\": \"AC-9.2\",\n     \"given\": \"A customer submits an invalid line, another organisation's address, a date earlier than permitted, or a product inactive for ordering.\",\n     \"when\": \"The customer places the order.\",\n     \"then\": \"The response status is 400 or 409 and no order row is created.\",\n     \"level\": \"api\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"id\": \"AC-9.3\",\n     \"given\": \"The serving warehouse has deployment-supplied cut-off, working-day, holiday, and local time-zone configuration.\",\n     \"when\": \"A customer requests an order delivery date before or after cut-off.\",\n     \"then\": \"The response record accepts no date earlier than the next working day before cut-off or the working day after that when submitted after cut-off.\",\n     \"level\": \"api\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"id\": \"AC-9.4\",\n     \"given\": \"An order is not yet Packed or has already reached Packed status.\",\n     \"when\": \"The customer attempts to change or cancel it.\",\n     \"then\": \"The response status and order status value reflect the applicable lifecycle rule, and successful cancellation returns the allocated quantity to available stock.\",\n     \"level\": \"api\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 1\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"REQ-10\",\n   \"ears\": \"The Meridian API shall allocate only released, physically available stock meeting customer minimum remaining shelf life, select earliest expiry first with the specified stability-budget tie-break, and apply complete-order, partial-order, back-order, and override rules.\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-2\",\n    \"I-3\",\n    \"Q-4\",\n    \"Q-5\"\n   ],\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"id\": \"AC-10.1\",\n     \"given\": \"Released stock is available for an order from its serving warehouse and has eligible lots.\",\n     \"when\": \"The order is allocated.\",\n     \"then\": \"The response record shows earliest-expiry eligible lots first, applies minimum remaining shelf life, uses greater stability-budget usage first for tied expiry dates, and exposes each allocation and outstanding quantity.\",\n     \"level\": \"api\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"id\": \"AC-10.2\",\n     \"given\": \"Suitable stock is insufficient for a partial order or any line of a complete-only order.\",\n     \"when\": \"Allocation is attempted.\",\n     \"then\": \"The partial order response shows allocated and outstanding quantities without over-allocating stock, while the complete-only order holds no stock until every line can be fully allocated.\",\n     \"level\": \"api\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"id\": \"AC-10.3\",\n     \"given\": \"Multiple orders are submitted concurrently against the same available handling units.\",\n     \"when\": \"The allocations are committed.\",\n     \"then\": \"The response records and stock list show no unit allocated to more than one order and total allocated quantity does not exceed physical available quantity.\",\n     \"level\": \"api\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"id\": \"AC-10.4\",\n     \"given\": \"A dispatcher submits an allocation override with a reason, without a reason, or to stock violating Released status or customer shelf life.\",\n     \"when\": \"The override operation is called.\",\n     \"then\": \"The valid response record includes the reason and changed allocation, while each invalid response status is 400 or 409 and the original allocation remains unchanged.\",\n     \"level\": \"api\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"id\": \"AC-10.5\",\n     \"given\": \"Suitable stock is released for waiting back orders.\",\n     \"when\": \"The allocation service updates affected orders.\",\n     \"then\": \"The order response records show oldest-first back-order allocation.\",\n     \"level\": \"api\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"id\": \"AC-10.6\",\n     \"given\": \"An older back order awaits suitable stock or a complete-only order cannot be fully allocated.\",\n     \"when\": \"Suitable stock is released or allocation is attempted.\",\n     \"then\": \"The response record shows eligible back orders filled in submission order and no stock held by the incomplete complete-only order.\",\n     \"level\": \"api\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 1\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"REQ-11\",\n   \"ears\": \"The Meridian API shall persist compatible box packing and route plans, enforce box and route qualification, and record driver loading, departure, synchronization, handover, refusal, and delivery-evidence operations.\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-2\",\n    \"I-3\",\n    \"Q-1\",\n    \"Q-2\",\n    \"Q-5\",\n    \"ASM-3\",\n    \"ASM-6\"\n   ],\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"id\": \"AC-11.1\",\n     \"given\": \"A Warehouse Operator submits a pack request for allocated stock.\",\n     \"when\": \"The requested box contains one logger, products with the same storage band, and a compatible box type.\",\n     \"then\": \"The response record contains the box, logger, lot quantities, operator, and seal time; a reused logger or incompatible packing response status is 409.\",\n     \"level\": \"api\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"id\": \"AC-11.2\",\n     \"given\": \"A dispatcher submits a route with date, vehicle, driver, ordered stops, and planned arrival times.\",\n     \"when\": \"The route is created, updated, or confirmed.\",\n     \"then\": \"The response record contains the requested route values and a conflicting driver or vehicle assignment returns status 409.\",\n     \"level\": \"api\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"id\": \"AC-11.3\",\n     \"given\": \"A route's packed box would exceed qualified duration less the configured safety margin at a planned arrival.\",\n     \"when\": \"The route confirmation operation is called.\",\n     \"then\": \"The response status is 409 and the response message identifies the box and qualification shortfall or duration overrun.\",\n     \"level\": \"api\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"id\": \"AC-11.4\",\n     \"given\": \"A driver calls route listing, route detail, scan, departure, or synchronization operations for the authenticated driver's route.\",\n     \"when\": \"The driver supplies contracted date, action identifiers, or route data.\",\n     \"then\": \"The response list or record contains only that driver's authorized route, ordered stops, expected boxes, scans, and departure state.\",\n     \"level\": \"api\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"id\": \"AC-11.5\",\n     \"given\": \"A driver synchronizes queued actions with distinct action identifiers or repeats an action identifier.\",\n     \"when\": \"The synchronization operation is called.\",\n     \"then\": \"The response record contains accepted and conflicting actions, and the resulting route history contains each accepted action only once.\",\n     \"level\": \"api\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"id\": \"AC-11.6\",\n     \"given\": \"A driver submits a handover with receiver, acknowledgement, signature, photo, completion time, and box delivery or refusal quantities.\",\n     \"when\": \"The handover operation is called and authorized delivery evidence is subsequently fetched.\",\n     \"then\": \"The response record and delivery-evidence response contain persisted evidence and quantities, and refused quantities retain the refusal reason.\",\n     \"level\": \"api\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"id\": \"AC-11.7\",\n     \"given\": \"A confirmed route is changed before its driver has left for the affected stop.\",\n     \"when\": \"A dispatcher updates the route schedule or stop order.\",\n     \"then\": \"The response record contains the changed schedule or stop order and an email call or driver-change event is recorded.\",\n     \"level\": \"api\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 1\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"REQ-12\",\n   \"ears\": \"The Meridian API shall process readings from contracted receipt logger uploads and the configured authenticated logger-gateway integration, expose temperature histories for contracted entity types, and persist available readings, gaps, excursions, tier-by-tier handling-unit budgets, related holds, and corrected history when readings arrive late or out of order.\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-2\",\n    \"I-3\",\n    \"Q-1\",\n    \"Q-3\",\n    \"ASM-4\",\n    \"ASM-8\",\n    \"ASM-10\"\n   ],\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"id\": \"AC-12.1\",\n     \"given\": \"A contracted receipt logger upload contains repeated, late, out-of-order, future-dated, or pre-sealing readings.\",\n     \"when\": \"The file is processed and temperature history is requested for its entity and date range.\",\n     \"then\": \"The response record places readings at their occurred times, stores a duplicate once, flags future and pre-sealing readings as excluded from calculations, and shows unavailable-reading gaps.\",\n     \"level\": \"api\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"id\": \"AC-12.2\",\n     \"given\": \"Three consecutive in-band readings follow an out-of-band reading in persisted history.\",\n     \"when\": \"The related temperature history and handling-unit record are requested.\",\n     \"then\": \"The response records show the excursion open from the first out-of-band reading until the third consecutive in-band reading and show time charged to each applicable tier.\",\n     \"level\": \"api\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"id\": \"AC-12.3\",\n     \"given\": \"A handling unit has excursion history or a late reading changes that history.\",\n     \"when\": \"The handling-unit or temperature-history operation is called after recalculation.\",\n     \"then\": \"The response record shows separate budgets for portions with different histories, updated remaining tier allowances, excursion links, holds, and an audit event for the correction.\",\n     \"level\": \"api\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"id\": \"AC-12.4\",\n     \"given\": \"An excursion begins, a tier allowance falls below 25 percent, a tier is exhausted, or a not-permitted range is reached.\",\n     \"when\": \"The triggering reading is received and processed.\",\n     \"then\": \"An email call is recorded within 120 seconds for the required driver when on-route, dispatcher, and warehouse Quality Officers, and affected stock response records have On Hold status pending a decision.\",\n     \"level\": \"job\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"id\": \"AC-12.5\",\n     \"given\": \"A logger has sent no reading for 15 minutes and its box is out for delivery.\",\n     \"when\": \"The silent-device check runs and temperature history is requested.\",\n     \"then\": \"The response record marks the device silent, shows the gap, and an alert email call is recorded.\",\n     \"level\": \"job\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"id\": \"AC-12.6\",\n     \"given\": \"A cold room or its temperature records are available.\",\n     \"when\": \"A caller lists cold rooms, retrieves a cold room, or requests temperature history for a room, box, lot, handling unit, or device.\",\n     \"then\": \"The response list or record contains the latest reading, status, gaps, alerts, history timestamps, and applicable band and excursion markers.\",\n     \"level\": \"api\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"id\": \"AC-12.7\",\n     \"given\": \"A handling unit has recorded temperature history with an interval containing no readings and a stored profile band.\",\n     \"when\": \"The caller fetches temperature history for the unit or its box, lot, device, or cold room.\",\n     \"then\": \"The response contains readings in recorded-time order, an explicit gap, and temperature-band and excursion fields for the requested interval.\",\n     \"level\": \"api\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"id\": \"AC-12.8\",\n     \"given\": \"The configured authenticated logger gateway sends a batch of readings for known devices, including duplicate, late, or out-of-order readings.\",\n     \"when\": \"The gateway integration processes the batch without exposing a new public HTTP operation.\",\n     \"then\": \"The persisted reading rows contain each valid reading once at its occurred time, and contracted temperature-history responses show the same ordered readings and calculated history regardless of batch arrival order.\",\n     \"level\": \"job\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 1\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"REQ-13\",\n   \"ears\": \"The Meridian API shall persist quality cases, signed proposals and decisions, superseding decisions, and destruction records, applying the required two-person quality approval and decision-history rules.\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-2\",\n    \"I-3\",\n    \"Q-2\",\n    \"Q-3\",\n    \"Q-5\",\n    \"Q-6\"\n   ],\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"id\": \"AC-13.1\",\n     \"given\": \"A Quality Officer submits a disposition proposal with disposition, reason, and identity confirmation.\",\n     \"when\": \"The proposal is retrieved or a decision is submitted by the proposing officer or an eligible different Quality Manager.\",\n     \"then\": \"The response record contains the proposal and actor, the same officer cannot approve it, and a different eligible manager's approval or return is recorded without replacing the proposal.\",\n     \"level\": \"api\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"id\": \"AC-13.2\",\n     \"given\": \"A quality decision exists and an authorized caller submits a separately signed superseding decision.\",\n     \"when\": \"The supersede operation is called.\",\n     \"then\": \"The response record contains the new decision and the earlier decision remains available in the returned decision history.\",\n     \"level\": \"api\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"id\": \"AC-13.3\",\n     \"given\": \"Rejected stock has a positive quantity to destroy.\",\n     \"when\": \"An authorized caller submits a destruction date, quantity, and witness.\",\n     \"then\": \"The response record contains those values and the destroyed quantity is removed from available stock.\",\n     \"level\": \"api\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"id\": \"AC-13.4\",\n     \"given\": \"A handling unit has tiered budget usage and a related quality case.\",\n     \"when\": \"An authorized Quality Officer fetches the unit and quality case.\",\n     \"then\": \"The response contains the used and remaining value for each tier and linked case telemetry and decision fields.\",\n     \"level\": \"api\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 1\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"REQ-14\",\n   \"ears\": \"The Meridian API shall persist signed recalls, trace selected lots through affected stock and delivery records, block affected stock still held, and record customer responses and signed closure or write-off decisions until quantities are accounted for.\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-2\",\n    \"I-3\",\n    \"Q-1\",\n    \"Q-2\",\n    \"Q-3\",\n    \"Q-5\",\n    \"Q-6\"\n   ],\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"id\": \"AC-14.1\",\n     \"given\": \"An eligible Quality Manager starts a signed recall for selected product lots.\",\n     \"when\": \"The recall is started and its record and trace are requested.\",\n     \"then\": \"The response records identify affected stock, warehouse locations, boxes, routes, deliveries, customer response progress, and recalled held stock is unavailable for allocation.\",\n     \"level\": \"api\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"id\": \"AC-14.2\",\n     \"given\": \"A customer submits or updates a recall response for an authorized delivery.\",\n     \"when\": \"The recall response operation is called.\",\n     \"then\": \"The response record contains on-hand, used, destroyed, and stated-disposition values and recall progress reflects the submitted quantities.\",\n     \"level\": \"api\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"id\": \"AC-14.3\",\n     \"given\": \"A recall has unaccounted quantity or all